(>> 3.1 Principles and Geometry of Multiview Projection) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Orthographic projection projects parallel perpendicular sight rays from an object to) Tj
T*
(mutually perpendicular viewing planes:) Tj
T*
(* The Three Principal Views: Front View \(Elevation\), Top View \(Plan\), and Side View) Tj
T*
(\(Profile view / End view\).) Tj
T*
(* Glass Box Concept: The object is imagined inside an imaginary glass box.) Tj
T*
(Projections of features onto the 6 walls are folded flat into a 2D plane.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 3.2 First Angle vs Third Angle Projection Systems) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* 1. First Angle Projection \(ISO / Indian BIS Standard\):) Tj
T*
(- Object is placed between Observer and Projection Plane \(Quadrant 1\).) Tj
T*
(- Front View is ABOVE the Top View.) Tj
T*
(- Left Side View is drawn on the RIGHT of Front View.) Tj
T*
(- Right Side View is drawn on the LEFT of Front View.) Tj
T*
(- Symbol: Truncated cone with small circle on right and front view trapezoid on left.) Tj
T*
(* 2. Third Angle Projection \(American ANSI Standard\):) Tj
T*
(- Projection Plane is placed between Observer and Object \(Quadrant 3, plane assumed) Tj
T*
(transparent\).) Tj
T*
(- Top View is ABOVE the Front View.) Tj
T*
(- Left Side View is drawn on the LEFT of Front View.) Tj
T*
(- Right Side View is drawn on the RIGHT of Front View.) Tj
T*
(- Symbol: Truncated cone with small circle on left and front view trapezoid on right.) Tj
T*
(* Comparative Summary Table:) Tj
T*
(- Parameter | First Angle System | Third Angle System) Tj
T*
(- Plane Transparency | Opaque planes behind object | Transparent planes in front of) Tj
T*
(object) Tj
T*
(- View Layout | Inverted \(Left on Right, Top below\) | Natural \(Left on Left, Top above\)) Tj
T*
(- Standard Code | BIS SP 46, ISO 128 | ASME Y14.3M) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
